                        <tr>
                           <th>Conclusion and Recommendations based on this report and previous findings known to us:</th>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>Renal function is mildly decreased (GFR 65 mL/min/1.73 m²), consistent with age-related decline. Urine albumin/creatinine ratio is at the upper limit of normal (28 mg/g), suggesting no significant albuminuria. Overall, results indicate stable, age-appropriate kidney function without evidence of significant renal impairment or proteinuria. Recommend continued monitoring.</td>
